message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "zynq-ternary-mobilenet-codesign: ternary-weight MobileNetV2 hardware/software co-design on Zynq UltraScale+"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hwz222/zynq-ternary-mobilenet-codesign"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Wei-Jhe
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Information Engineering, National Central University, Taiwan"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - ternary weight networks
  - human pose estimation
  - hardware/software co-design
  - MobileNetV2
  - Zynq UltraScale+
  - hardware accelerator
abstract: >-
  A hardware/software co-design of a ternary-weight MobileNetV2 on a Zynq UltraScale+ MPSoC (ALINX
  AXU2CGB, XCZU2CG): a fused, row-streaming Verilog accelerator in the PL and Linux control software
  on the ARM PS. Pose estimation is the reference task with board results; detection, segmentation
  and depth models for the same fixed network are included with host results. The release contains
  the RTL and testbenches, a bit-exact C reference, Vivado and PetaLinux build scripts, board
  software, and the training, quantisation and export code.
